# Caddy reverse proxy with automatic HTTPS in front of addresses_api.
#
# Behaviour depends on the SERVER_NAME env var:
#   • SERVER_NAME=localhost (default) — Caddy issues a cert from its
#     internal CA. Browsers will warn unless you install Caddy's root
#     cert into your trust store. Good for dev.
#
#   • SERVER_NAME=<real public hostname> — Caddy auto-fetches a
#     Let's Encrypt cert via ACME and renews it transparently. Requires
#     ports 80 + 443 reachable from the public internet, with DNS
#     pointing the hostname here.
#
# SERVER_NAME also accepts multiple space-separated hostnames, e.g.
# "example.com www.example.com" — Caddy issues a single SAN cert for all.
#
# Cert state is persisted in the caddy_data named volume so renewals
# survive container rebuilds.

{$SERVER_NAME:localhost} {
    reverse_proxy addresses_api:{$API_PORT:8000}
}
